  "body": "Part of #361. The lathe case the issue names (Capto / KM holders, often not symmetric).\n\n**Today:** the lathe stock sim does not judge the holder (`crates/app/src/stock_sim_lathe.rs`: \"the holder are not ...\"). Only the insert is judged.\n\n**Proposed:**\n- **Collision rule.** The part spins, so a body point at (x, y, z) in the machine's ZX frame collides with the stock if its radial distance from the spindle axis is less than the stock's radius at that z.\n- **Body clearance.** From the tool body (#368 gives the import and placement), derive a minimum-radial-distance profile along Z.\n- **Judging.** Judge that profile against the revolved in-process stock along each move, as a protected-move finding that blocks the post.\n- **Fallback.** A turning tool without a body keeps today's behaviour, plus one named \"holder not judged\" note.\n\n**Done means:** a modelled offset holder that rubs the shoulder of a stepped part is caught; the same move without a body is unchanged; goldens for one OD and one ID (boring bar) case.\n\nDepends on the body import from #368.\n\n",
